tags: linux-amd64, linux/amd64, amd64, x86_64

A Linux virtual machine on x86-64, 64-bit. The software of the service runs as Linux
processes in a guest with its own kernel. It does not share the kernel of the host.

The node guarantees only the instructions of the baseline level of x86-64
(x86-64-v1). Software that needs a higher level (for example AVX2 of x86-64-v3) can
fail. Another level is another architecture, with another formal. The node can run the
guest natively or with an emulator: the benchmarks of the node show the difference.

The setting guest-kernel of Container.Init selects the kernel (0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:9c03c66a3776b9ce1260b15aca7f0525ea6542092800cd4a23e07eda60cbeb97).
With no such setting, the node selects the kernel.

Who is bound: the node that runs the service. An architecture has no value.

=== formal
abi=the Linux system call interface of x86-64, 64-bit (not x32)
class=architecture
isa=x86-64-v1: only the instructions of the baseline level of x86-64
kernel=the node boots a Linux guest kernel in a virtual machine for each instance; the processes of the instance do not share the kernel of the host
